msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "A unit of the landscape (UT, UT0, another district) or a site (a LocationNodeGroup of level sito, virtual or not) belongs to a DISTRICT (DistrictNode, node datamodel 1.6.41). An interpretation of PERTINENCE, not a geometric fact: the villa is in its fundus because somebody argues it, not because two polygons overlap — the overlap is computed from the geometries, never written. Declared, so signed and argued by its paradata like any declaration. m:n: a unit may belong to several districts (the villa in its fundus and in the territory of the town); a district may be in another district (the Forum in Pompeii) with the same edge. The VALIDITY in time of a membership is DERIVED as the intersection of the two lives (as for a functional unit), computed by s3dgraphy.landscape, never written. New in 1.6.53 (MICRO-LANDSCAPE-ONTOLOGIA, D-LG6): is\\_in\\_location says WHAT NAMED PLACE a thing is in (an atemporal identity), is\\_part\\_of is physical containment, is\\_in\\_functional\\_unit what a set of units IS; none says the pertinence of a site to a declared portion of territory that has a time of its own."
msgstr ""

